00:39:45,860 --> 00:39:48,620
God, I don't deserve this. This is such a good gift from you.

369
00:39:48,620 --> 00:39:55,360
Or are you just enjoying pleasure, earthly pleasure?

370
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:13,940
I want to end this part of the message reading this long quote from a book that I've come back to over and over and over again.

371
00:40:13,940 --> 00:40:16,920
I've read it, like, I've had to buy three copies of this thing because I always lose it.

372
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:22,260
It's not a popular book, so the author is probably like, sweet.

373
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:25,600
Somebody bought my book again. It's like, no, Ryan bought it again.

374
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:29,320
You didn't sell a new copy. You just, Ryan bought it again.

375
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:33,320
It's about, yeah.

376
00:40:34,760 --> 00:40:43,520
I just, I just, I just spent some time yesterday giving my mom a beautiful compliment to herself and to people in front of her.

377
00:40:43,520 --> 00:40:46,180
That, well, behind her back, I complimented her.

378
00:40:46,180 --> 00:40:49,200
So, I don't feel so guilty making a joke right now.

379
00:40:52,320 --> 00:40:54,620
One time we were driving home at about 9 p.m.

380
00:40:54,620 --> 00:40:57,600
9 p.m.

381
00:40:57,600 --> 00:40:59,660
Let me say it again, 9 p.m.

382
00:40:59,660 --> 00:41:06,860
And I mean, the moon was magnificent.

383
00:41:06,860 --> 00:41:10,860
Large, orange tint.

384
00:41:10,860 --> 00:41:11,760
I mean, beautiful.

385
00:41:13,140 --> 00:41:20,020
And my mom, God love her, from the front of the car, she said, the moon is beautiful.

386
00:41:20,020 --> 00:41:23,580
Or is that the sun?

387
00:41:23,580 --> 00:41:30,900
And I mean, we'll never let her live that down to this day.

388
00:41:30,900 --> 00:41:32,540
It was probably like 7.30.

389
00:41:32,540 --> 00:41:36,040
So, like, it's become later and later the more we tell the story.

390
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:37,460
When I tell it, it's 9 o'clock.

391
00:41:41,180 --> 00:41:50,340
But that's, the illustration this author uses is this idea that oftentimes we, the moon is just a reflection from the light of the sun.

392
00:41:50,340 --> 00:41:59,200
And oftentimes, like, we can live our lives just obsessed with the reflection of God's goodness while we're missing out on God himself.

393
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:01,980
Let me read this.

394
00:42:01,980 --> 00:42:06,420
I am reminded of the difference between the sun and the moon.

395
00:42:07,360 --> 00:42:11,600
If all you had ever seen was a full moon, you might think it was the sun.

396
00:42:11,600 --> 00:42:13,620
Mom.

397
00:42:13,620 --> 00:42:18,340
After all, there are great similarities.

398
00:42:18,340 --> 00:42:20,240
A full moon is big and bright.

399
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:26,740
If you thought that that was all there was, imagine what it would be like to suddenly see the sun in all of its brilliance.

400
00:42:26,740 --> 00:42:32,600
The moon would be usurped in your evaluation by something more magnificently brilliant and beautiful.

401
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:35,760
You would never look at the moon the same way again.

402
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:43,440
There would still be much to enjoy about the moonlight, but it would be enjoyed for what it is, a reflected light.

403
00:42:43,440 --> 00:42:49,440
Every created pleasure and beauty that we have ever enjoyed in this world is like moonlight.

404
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:54,520
Void of any comparison, they seem like the best this life has to offer.

405
00:42:55,220 --> 00:43:00,500
But through the gospel and the Holy Spirit, we have seen the radiant glory of the beautiful one, Christ.

406
00:43:00,500 --> 00:43:06,340
And this changes our perspective on the pleasure of moonlight beauty.

407
00:43:06,340 --> 00:43:11,220
We used to worship reflections, but through the gospel and the Holy Spirit, we discern a better beauty.

408
00:43:11,220 --> 00:43:16,820
Until we see the beauty of Christ, we will never see the true beauty of anything else.

409
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:24,920
And once we discern his glory, we enjoy the moonlight of created beauties all the more because they remind us of him.

410
00:43:24,920 --> 00:43:29,460
In fact, now we enjoy the moon because we love the sun.

411
00:43:29,460 --> 00:43:32,400
Jesus is the person we love.

412
00:43:32,400 --> 00:43:34,220
The created world is his reflection.

413
00:43:34,220 --> 00:43:42,640
If we love him, we will love every resemblance of him and see every good and true in the universe as a picture of him.

414
00:43:43,420 --> 00:43:46,980
The universe is all about him.

415
00:43:46,980 --> 00:43:52,800
And Christians have the joy of seeing him in all the created wonders of this world.

416
00:43:52,800 --> 00:44:04,860
This is a spirit-enabled perspective that turns wonders, sensory experience of beauty into occasions for joy, reflection, and worship.

417
00:44:04,860 --> 00:44:13,240
Sabbath is a day set apart for us to enjoy God's gifts and grow and surrender to him.

418
00:44:13,300 --> 00:44:13,620
Let's pray.

419
00:44:13,620 --> 00:44:19,200
Father in heaven, you're so good.

420
00:44:19,200 --> 00:44:22,480
You give such good gifts.

421
00:44:22,480 --> 00:44:32,280
And God, the temptation for all of us, no matter how much time we spent in the prayer closet this morning,

422
00:44:32,280 --> 00:44:38,840
the temptation for all of us is to leave your presence and grasp onto earthly things.

423
00:44:40,320 --> 00:44:42,920
God, today, give us eyes to see our idolatry.

424
00:44:42,920 --> 00:44:51,000
Most of us are gonna turn on a football game tonight

425
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:57,460
that has probably six hours of pre-game coverage

426
00:44:57,460 --> 00:45:05,100
because we're worshipers.

427
00:45:05,100 --> 00:45:13,200
God, we're longing to find hope and satisfaction, security, and joy.

428
00:45:13,980 --> 00:45:16,340
And we look for it in such silly places.

429
00:45:16,340 --> 00:45:29,980
God, as we watch a game tonight that's fun and entertaining, may we view it as such.

430
00:45:33,620 --> 00:45:37,400
Lead us away from our idolatry and into growing surrender to you.

431
00:45:37,400 --> 00:45:44,520
God, may we be a countercultural community with different loyalties.

432
00:45:52,080 --> 00:45:53,400
God, teach us to surrender.

433
00:45:53,400 --> 00:45:58,120
Help us to receive your grace and your forgiveness when we don't.

434
00:45:58,120 --> 00:46:03,140
There is no condemnation for those of us who are in Christ.

435
00:46:03,140 --> 00:46:07,940
God, many of us in this room are probably aware of so many areas where we are idolaters, myself included.

436
00:46:10,340 --> 00:46:14,640
As you bring those things to our minds, may the result not be guilt and shame.

437
00:46:14,640 --> 00:46:20,160
May the result be gratitude and surrender.

438
00:46:20,160 --> 00:46:25,080
God, thank you for showing me the ways in which I have overinvested in temporary things.

439
00:46:25,080 --> 00:46:31,840
Moving forward, give me the strength and the ability to receive surrender.

440
00:46:35,220 --> 00:46:35,940
We love you.

441
00:46:35,940 --> 00:46:37,820
In Jesus' name I pray.

442
00:46:37,820 --> 00:46:38,980
Amen.

443
00:46:38,980 --> 00:46:48,800
We're going to take communion together, if you've got some on your way in.
